				1505,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(DOCSV+FRALIAS): replace /tmp sentinel fallback and add StripFileUriScheme to legacy aliases\n\nDOCSV — Documents.rs:\n- Document.Save and Document.SaveAs previously fell back to\n  `file:///tmp/test.txt` when the incoming URI was empty or unparseable.\n  This caused SaveDocument/SaveDocumentAs to silently operate on the\n  wrong file. Both handlers now return Err(...) for an empty URI, and\n  use Url::parse(...).map_err(...) for an invalid one, matching the\n  pattern used in Debug.Start.\n\nFRALIAS — FileReadAlias.rs:\n- The legacy `openDocument`, `readFile`, and `stat` routes extracted the\n  path string and passed it directly to PathBuf::from without calling\n  StripFileUriScheme. Cocoon sends full `file:///` URIs through these\n  routes; without stripping, PathBuf roots at the literal scheme string\n  and every read 404s. Added StripFileUriScheme (imported from\n  FileSystem.rs's module — inlined here since it lives in a sibling\n  module) and applied it before PathBuf construction. Also added\n  empty-path guard matching the FileSystem.* contract.",
			"SHA": "2ebd1eb38a2618ebaef48744f7558991ea1ec115"
		},
